    "result_text": "The build is green. Let me summarize what I changed.\n\n## Summary\n\nRedesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is `<REGION>-<HASH8>` and every value derived from it moved to the new region-and-hash identity. **Build passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.**\n\n### The new identity\n\nNew utility **`OwnerCustomerCode`** (`rest/function/owner/OwnerCustomerCode.java`) centralizes the derivation:\n- **REGION** \u2014 from the postcode via the region ranges (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), falling back to the city\u2192region table, else `UNKNOWN`.\n- **HASH8** \u2014 first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`, where the telephone is normalized to E.164 (reusing `E164Telephone`), matching the acceptance test's `shaHex(...)` ground truth.\n- No sequence number \u2014 the old per-city `count()` over `findAll()` is gone.\n\n### Everything built from `customerCode` follows\n\n- **`AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 rewritten to emit `<REGION>-<HASH8>`; no longer needs `OwnerRepository`. (No YAML change needed \u2014 the step still resolves.)\n- **Membership number** (`OwnerMapper.toMembershipNumber`) and **check digit** (`toCheckDigit`, Luhn) already read the `customerCode` string, so they now build on the new identity automatically \u2014 e.g. `NSW-1A2B3C4D-M26`.\n- **Audit record** (`AuditOwnerCreated`) already logs `customerCode`; the log now shows the new form (verified: `AUDIT - Owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E ...`).\n- **Locality** (`OwnerMapper.toLocality`) \u2014 now the REGION segment of the `customerCode` (the substring before the dash), i.e. derived from the identity rather than recomputed independently; falls back to direct region derivation only for unmigrated owners with no customer code.\n\n### Docs\n\nUpdated the `openapi.yml` descriptions/examples for `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality`, plus the relevant javadocs, to describe the region-and-hash format.\n\nOne thing worth noting: `customerCode` uniqueness now rests on `(telephone, lastName)` per region rather than a monotonic sequence. That's inherent to the spec (SHA-256 over telephone+lastName); two owners with the same last name, same normalized telephone, and same region would collide \u2014 but that combination is already blocked upstream by the duplicate-identity check on telephone.",
